From 8209f4adcde08d225f56269e608ccd5f6704cd70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lennart Poettering <lennart@poettering.net>
Date: Thu, 9 Oct 2025 11:04:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] resolved: add hook api

This introduces /run/systemd/resolve.hook/ as a new directory that local
(privileged) programs can bind a Varlink socket into. If they do they'll
get a method call for each attempted resolved lookup, which they can
then either process themselves (and generate new records for, or return
errors to block stuff) or let pass so that the regular resolution is
done.

Usecase for this is primarily two things:

1. in machined we can add local resolution of machine names to their IP
   addresses, similar in fashion to nss-mymachines, but working also if
   the non-NSS interfaces to name resolution are used, i.e. the local
   DNS responder. In fact, I think we should eventually remove
   nss-mymachines from our tree, as soon as this code in resolved is
   setlled.

2. in networkd we can add local resolution of names specified in DHCP
   leases we hand out.

But beyond that there should be many other uses, for example people
could write "dns firewalls" with this if they like where they
dynamically block certain names from resolution.

Fixes: #8518

Also contains the follow-up upstream fix from commit
dfc4658b2f8089fc65d3becbbc97b5926871a644 ("resolved: fix hook filter
connection lifecycle"):

    Keep the replacement filter connection after a disconnect instead of
    falling through to terminate and immediately destroying it. Clear the
    previous filter so stale domains or label limits cannot suppress queries
    while the replacement filter reply is pending.

    Retry missing filter connections on later lookups before the unchanged
    directory shortcut. This also recovers socket-activated hooks whose socket
    remains present. Apply the existing rate limit in hook_acquire_filter()
    so all acquisition paths share it, and report only the first suppressed
    attempt per window.

    Stop filter monitoring when unlinking a hook. A pending query can retain
    the Hook after its manager has been cleared; a subsequent filter
    disconnect would otherwise try to reconnect and fail assert(h->manager).
    The pending query retains its separate connection and can still complete.

[v255 backport note: this backport was adapted to the systemd v255.2 API,
which predates the public sd-varlink and sd-json APIs used by the upstream
version of this commit:
- sd_varlink_*() calls were mapped onto the internal varlink_*() API
  (src/shared/varlink.h), sd_json_*() onto the JsonVariant/json_*() API
  (src/shared/json.h). SD_JSON_ALLOW_EXTENSIONS became JSON_PERMISSIVE,
  SD_JSON_NULLABLE has no v255 equivalent and is handled in the dispatch
  callbacks instead.
- src/resolve/resolved-forward.h does not exist in v255.2; the required
  forward declarations live in src/resolve/resolved-hook.h and
  resolved-dns-query.h.
- src/shared/resolved-def.h is src/resolve/resolved-def.h in v255.2.
- src/resolve/resolved-varlink.c has no resolve_service_all_complete() in
  v255.2 (the varlink service shares the bus implementation), so that part
  of the upstream commit was dropped.
- src/resolve/test-dns-query.c does not exist in v255.2, so the test
  hermeticity hunk (SYSTEMD_RESOLVED_HOOK=0) was dropped.
- v255.2's varlink IDL macros (VARLINK_DEFINE_*) have no field/interface
  comments and no way to mark a method as supporting the "more" flag; those
  annotations were dropped. ResourceKey/ResourceRecord are shared with the
  io.systemd.Resolve.Monitor interface, so they are referenced via extern
  declarations instead of being defined again.]

---
